      <div class="col-sm-6 col-md-5 custom-column-gap">
        <h3>Why become a mentor?</h3>
        <p>Becoming a mentor is not just rewarding for the person you guide, but it’s a transformative experience for you as well.</p>
        <p><strong>Making a Difference:</strong> You have the chance to positively impact someone's life by sharing your knowledge, experience, and wisdom.</p>
        <p><strong>Personal Growth:</strong> Mentoring often deepens your own understanding of your field or skills.</p>
        <p><strong>Strengthening Leadership Skills:</strong> As a mentor, you develop abilities like patience, active listening, empathy, and strategic thinking.</p>
        <p><strong>Creating a Legacy:</strong> Helping someone succeed creates a ripple effect beyond just one person.</p>
        <p><strong>Building Relationships:</strong> Mentorship fosters deep connections that can last a lifetime.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="col-sm-6 col-md-5">
        <h3>Why become a mentee?</h3>
        <p>Becoming a mentee is an incredible opportunity for personal and professional growth.</p>
        <p><strong>Learning from Experience:</strong> A mentor has often walked the path you're on and can share insights.</p>
        <p><strong>Expanding Your Perspective:</strong> Mentors can introduce you to new ideas, ways of thinking, or approaches.</p>
        <p><strong>Accelerating Your Development:</strong> With guidance, you can progress more quickly in your goals.</p>
        <p><strong>Building Confidence:</strong> A mentor's encouragement and feedback can boost your self-assurance.</p>
        <p><strong>Networking Opportunities:</strong> Mentors often have extensive networks and can connect you to valuable resources.</p>
        <p><strong>Personalized Guidance:</strong> Unlike general advice, a mentor's support is tailored to your unique aspirations.</p>
      </div>
